From c5c1b716eae5649a27607d52362592f228d256fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard Levitte <levitte@openssl.foundation>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 10:22:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix potential double-free in dh_finish()
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

dh_finish() (the default DH method's finish slot) frees the cached
Montgomery context, dh->method_mont_p, without NULLing the pointer.
Once the cache has been warmed, a subsequent finish call — e.g. via
DH_free() after DH_set_method() — frees it again.

NULL the pointer after freeing.

Fixes: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/issues/32541
Assisted-by: Pi:moonshotai/kimi-k3
Signed-off-by: Richard Levitte <levitte@openssl.foundation>
Reviewed-by: Dmitry Belyavskiy <beldmit@gmail.com>
Reviewed-by: Mounir Idrassi <mounir.idrassi@idrix.fr>
Merge-date: Tue Oct 27 12:15:36 2026
Merged-from: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/32602
Cherry-picked-from: 7fd4fb5084cfdda14925e6f997fe1e0a2fd88791
---
 crypto/dh/dh_key.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/crypto/dh/dh_key.c b/crypto/dh/dh_key.c
index 2d9f7a81..7fbe8d11 100644
--- a/crypto/dh/dh_key.c
+++ b/crypto/dh/dh_key.c
@@ -207,6 +207,7 @@ static int dh_init(DH *dh)
 static int dh_finish(DH *dh)
 {
     BN_MONT_CTX_free(dh->method_mont_p);
+    dh->method_mont_p = NULL;
     return 1;
 }
 
